\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Ultimate Button\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb200\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 Driver Properties
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf0 Button Name:
\f3\b0  Read-only property displaying the name that was last set on the proxy.\

\f2\b Brightness:
\f3\b0  Value between 0 and 255.\

\f2\b Text Color:
\f3\b0  The color of the text of the button.\

\f2\b Background Color:
\f3\b0  The color of the background of the button.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs26 \cf0 Using the Driver\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs22 \cf0 There are three stages to using the driver.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Making it visible\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0 \cf0 Select each room you want the button to be visible in in turn.  Now for the room select the Navigator tab and the Experience Menu you require.  Note that Experience Buttons cannot be shown under Lights or Shades.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Performing the Action\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0 \cf0 In Custom Programming select the button under Device Events.  A single Selected (On) event is available.  Choose this and then add in the custom programming you want to execute when the customer selects the button on the UI.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Feedback (Optional)\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0 \cf0 If you want to provide feedback on the button then you can add custom programming using the Device Actions.  A Device Specific Command is available \'91Set State\'92.  This enables you to set the icon state on the UI either to the Default (Off) or Selected (On) state.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

